Notebook[{Cell["Exact rotation closure and source-degree audit", "Title"], 
  Cell["Version-3 human notation guide (documentation only; no Input cell is \
changed). In the compact solution and verifier notebooks: x=r^2; q1,q2,q3 are \
the harmonic parameters mu1,mu2,mu3, not normalized conserved charges; jrot \
is the rotation parameter j; U1,U2,U3 are the electric corrections delta u_I; \
B1,B2,B3 are the gauge-covariant fibre corrections; Om is delta omega; Ft, \
Gr, and Sq are the temporal warp, radial warp, and squashing corrections; P \
and S are delta p and delta s, where X1=exp(2p/3-s), X2=exp(2p/3+s), and \
X3=exp(-4p/3). Physical quantities are Q_I=Pi mu_I/(4 G5) and J1=J2=Pi j/(4 \
G5). See the report section 'Human-readable notation and result at a glance' \
for the full dictionary.", "Text"], Cell["PACKAGE-V1 SUPERSESSION NOTICE: \
Historical OPEN, NOT COMPUTED, or NOT CLAIMED values retained later in this \
notebook describe the evidence available when this notebook was first sealed; \
they are not the current package-v1 claim ledger. Current package-v1 \
certificates supersede them as follows: GenericStatic -> notebook 13; \
GenericWaldAndPhysicalNormalization -> notebook 14; HorizonRegularity -> \
notebook 15; CassaniHeteroticEq331 -> notebook 16; PageRadialIdentity -> \
notebook 17. Only the corrected ten-dimensional-to-five-dimensional \
field-by-field map remains open/conditional.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Purpose: document why the finite rotation polynomial is exhaustive at \
first order in lambda3. This concise notebook replays the archived closure \
ledger; notebook 12 is the self-contained true from-EOM verifier that \
recomputes every residual and classifies the two coefficient members \
separately.", "Text"], Cell["1. Finite correction ansatz", "Section"], 
  Cell[BoxData["ClearAll[\"Global`*\"]; evenCorrection=f0[x]+jrot^2 f2[x]; \
oddCorrection=jrot g1[x]+jrot^3 g3[x]; \
rotationAnsatz=<|\"Even\"->evenCorrection,\"Odd\"->oddCorrection,\"HighestEve\
nFieldPower\"->2,\"HighestOddFieldPower\"->3|>; rotationAnsatz"], "Input"], 
  Cell["2. Compression scale and recorded coefficient closure", "Section"], 
  Cell["The count tables are provenance records from coefficient extraction. \
The zero arrays and evidence classes replay the archived full-substitution \
ledger and are not a from-EOM calculation. For the latter, evaluate notebook \
12, which contains the literal equations, full sources, and separate \
homogeneous/source coefficient members.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData["metricJ2CompressionCounts=<|\"f\"-><|\"OriginalTerms\"->25042\
,\"SelectedJ2Terms\"->7671,\"CompactNumeratorMonomials\"->511|>,\"gr\"-><|\"O\
riginalTerms\"->13230,\"SelectedJ2Terms\"->3518,\"CompactNumeratorMonomials\"\
->343|>,\"hr\"-><|\"OriginalTerms\"->31027,\"SelectedJ2Terms\"->10978,\"Compa\
