s\"->closureReplayPass|>"], "Input"], 
  Cell["3. Three different rotation-degree statements", "Section"], 
  Cell["The raw two-derivative homogeneous operators have degree at most two \
in even equations and at most one in odd equations. After the finite closed \
solution is inserted, their homogeneous contributions can reach degree four \
and three, respectively. The complete four-derivative sources have the \
equation-by-equation degrees below: omega reaches seven, while hr and \
squashing reach eight. These distinctions replace the earlier shorthand that \
grouped only small source sectors.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData["rawHomogeneousOperatorDegrees=<|\"u1\"->2,\"u2\"->2,\"u3\"->2\
,\"v1\"->1,\"v2\"->1,\"v3\"->1,\"p\"->2,\"s\"->2,\"f\"->2,\"gr\"->2,\"hr\"->2\
,\"squ\"->2,\"omega\"->1|>; \
fullSourceDegrees=<|\"u1\"->4,\"u2\"->4,\"u3\"->4,\"v1\"->3,\"v2\"->3,\"v3\"-\
>3,\"p\"->4,\"s\"->2,\"f\"->6,\"gr\"->6,\"hr\"->8,\"squ\"->8,\"omega\"->7|>; \
postSolutionHomogeneousBounds=<|\"EvenMaximum\"->4,\"OddMaximum\"->3|>; \
expectedClosureCounts=<|\"j4Even\"->9,\"j5Odd\"->4,\"j6Even\"->9,\"j7Odd\"->4\
,\"j8Even\"->9|>; recordedClosureCounts=Map[Length,recordedClosureResiduals]; \
degreeAuditPass=TrueQ[Max[Values@KeyTake[rawHomogeneousOperatorDegrees,{\"u1\
\",\"u2\",\"u3\",\"p\",\"s\",\"f\",\"gr\",\"hr\",\"squ\"}]]===2&&Max[Values@K\
eyTake[rawHomogeneousOperatorDegrees,{\"v1\",\"v2\",\"v3\",\"omega\"}]]===1&&\
Max[Values[fullSourceDegrees]]===8&&fullSourceDegrees[\"omega\"]===7&&postSol\
utionHomogeneousBounds===<|\"EvenMaximum\"->4,\"OddMaximum\"->3|>&&recordedCl\
osureCounts===expectedClosureCounts]; \
exactInRotationReplayPass=TrueQ[closureReplayPass&&recordedClassPass&&degreeA\
uditPass]; \
<|\"RawHomogeneousOperatorDegrees\"->rawHomogeneousOperatorDegrees,\"FullSour\
ceDegrees\"->fullSourceDegrees,\"PostSolutionHomogeneousBounds\"->postSolutio\
nHomogeneousBounds,\"ClosureCounts\"->recordedClosureCounts,\"RecordedClassCo\
unts\"->recordedClassCounts,\"DegreeAuditPass\"->degreeAuditPass,\"ExactInRot\
ationRecordedLedgerPass\"->exactInRotationReplayPass|>"], "Input"], 
  Cell["4. Evidence boundary", "Section"], Cell["Notebook 10 is a compact \
ledger and degree audit. Notebook 12 performs the decisive computation: exact \
O(j), O(j^2), and O(j^3) substitutions, five nontrivial j^4 \
homogeneous/source cancellations in u1, u2, u3, p, and f, and 30 canonical \
zero/zero absence checks (the other four j^4 equations and all j^5-j^8 \
records). All 35 residual coefficients vanish. The generic static metric \
sector is supported by exact-rational samples rather than an arbitrary-charge \
symbolic theorem. Generic higher-derivative Wald angular momentum, the \
rotating heterotic field map, and invariant horizon regularity remain open.", 
   "Text"], Cell[BoxData["<|\"ConciseLedgerPass\"->exactInRotationReplayPass,\
\"RecordedNontrivialCancellationCount\"->Lookup[recordedClassCounts,\"NONTRIV\
IAL_CANCELLATION\",0],\"RecordedAbsenceZeroZeroCount\"->Lookup[recordedClassC\
ounts,\"ABSENCE_ZERO_ZERO\",0],\"TrueFromEOMVerifier\"->\"12_True_FromEOM_Exa\
ctInJ_Verifier.nb\",\"GenericStaticMetricSymbolicProof\"->\"NOT \
CLAIMED\",\"GenericWaldJ4\"->\"NOT \
COMPUTED\",\"HeteroticFieldMap\"->\"OPEN\",\"InvariantHorizonRegularity\"->\"\
OPEN\"|>"], "Input"], Cell["Conclusion: the rotation-dependent correction is \
exact in jrot at first order in lambda3, as proved by notebook 12. No claim \
is made about O(lambda3^2). The identification lambda3=alpha'/8 is a \
normalization inherited from the static embedding until the rotating \
five-to-ten-dimensional field map is completed.", "Text"]}, 
